<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell 22 points to 1,292.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell 22 points to 1,292.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,292 today from 1,314 on April 22, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1311    11.900	  1325    12.025</p>
<p>   1a   1320 10000.000	  1342 10163.000</p>
<p>   2    1540    22.000	  1555    22.219</p>
<p>   2a   1494 12250.000	  1540 12631.000</p>
<p>   3    1397    12.893	  1440    13.281</p>
<p>   3a   1242  9800.000	  1295 10219.000</p>
